          "english": "It is not controversial to say that an unhealthy diet causes bad health. Nor are the basic elements of healthy eating disputed. Obesity raises susceptibility to cancer, and Britain is the sixth most obese country on Earth. That is a public health emergency. But naming the problem is the easy part. No one disputes the costs in quality of life and depleted health budgets of an obese population, but the quest for solutions gets diverted by ideological arguments around responsibility and choice. And the water is muddied by lobbying from the industries that profit from consumption of obesity-inducing products.",
          "chinese": "说不健康的饮食会导致健康状况恶化，并无争议。健康饮食的基本要素同样没有争议。肥胖会增加罹患癌症的易感性，而英国是全球肥胖程度排名第六的国家。这是一场公共卫生紧急事件。但指出问题所在是容易的部分。没有人否认肥胖人口会在生活质量和日益枯竭的卫生预算方面造成代价，但围绕责任和选择的意识形态争论使人们寻求解决方案的努力偏离了方向。而那些从消费导致肥胖的产品中获利的行业游说，也使问题变得更加混乱。",
